        "widgetData": {
          "content": "<p>Bobby Madley has been confirmed as the match referee for Saturday's Sky Bet League One fixture between County and Reading at Edgeley Park.</p>\n<p>The official has refereed County on two previous occasions, overseeing our 0-0 draw away at Lincoln City in October 2010, as well as our 1-1 draw at Luton Town in League One last season.</p>\n<p>He has also officiated opponents Reading on four previous occasions, most recently in December 2023 for their 1-1 draw away at Lincoln City in League One.</p>\n<p>Madley took charge of 21 first-team fixtures across all competitions during the 2025/26 campaign, covering the Championship, League One and League Two, as well as the Carabao Cup. In that time, he issued a total of 76 yellow cards and four red cards, whilst awarding two penalty kicks.</p>\n<p>Across the eight games he has overseen so far this season, covering the Championship and Carabao Cup, he has shown 30 yellows and one red, whilst awarding two penalties to date. His most recent fixture came in the Championship last Saturday, when he took charge of QPR's 2-1 win at home to Lincoln City.</p>\n<p>The Assistant Referees on Saturday will be Richard Woodward and Matthew Sowerby, with Leigh Doughty on Fourth Official duties at Edgeley Park.</p>",
